KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ parameter of incomplete type: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ complete type: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [expr.prim.req.general]/5, [dcl.fct]/13: substituting
wrapper<incomplete> into the parameter-declarations `I a, I b' of the
requires-expression yields parameters of an incomplete class type, which
makes the requires-expression false.  The front end evaluates only the
requirement `a - b', which a declared operator- satisfies.  g++ 13 and
clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
